This function uses a nested loop to iterate through all possible divisors of each number in the input array. It first checks if the number is less than or equal to 1, which are not considered prime by most definitions, and skips over them. Then it loops through all integers from 2 up to the square root of the number being checked (inclusive), looking for a factor. If a factor is found, it breaks out of the inner loop and moves on to the next number in the array. If none were found, the number must be a prime number and we print it to the console. 

